<title>CHINA: CHINA FARM BUDGET 93.8 BILLION YUAN IN 1997.</title>
<headline>CHINA FARM BUDGET 93.8 BILLION YUAN IN 1997.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's budget for its huge farm sector will swell by 26.8 percent, or 20 billion yuan, in 1997 to 93.8 billion yuan, the China Economic Times said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Direct government investment in agriculture would hit 48.8 billion yuan this year while expenditures for other projects related to the farm sector would boost spending to 93.8 billion yuan, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>Channels for investment in agriculture had increased because many local governments were encouraging big and medium-sized industrial enterprises to enter the sector, it said but gave no further details.</p>
<p>($1=8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>-- Beijing newsroom (86-10) 6532-1921</p>
</text>
